{
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": false
  },
  "name": "Shopify new product to AI product video ad with Sisif",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c96440ae-fa40-44f0-97c4-24e8a7bef91a",
      "name": "Setup Instructions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1500,
        -700
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Turn new Shopify products into AI product video ads with Sisif\n\n### Who it's for\nShopify merchants and e-commerce teams who want a short motion video on every new product page without a video shoot.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Shopify Trigger** fires when a product is created.\n2. The main product image and copy are extracted. Products without an image are skipped.\n3. An AI model writes a short camera/motion prompt for that product.\n4. **Sisif** animates the product photo into a 5-second portrait MP4 (image-to-video).\n5. The workflow polls every 30 s until the video is `READY`, stops on `ERROR`/`REFUNDED`, and times out after 40 checks.\n6. The MP4 is uploaded to Shopify with a staged upload and added to the product as media (Admin GraphQL API). If any Shopify step fails, the MP4 is saved to Google Drive instead.\n7. A Slack message reports the result.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Sisif API key at https://sisif.ai/users/api-keys/ and add it in n8n as a **Bearer Auth** credential. Select it on **Generate Video from Image** and **Check Video Status**.\n2. Create a Shopify custom app with `read_products` and `write_products` scopes, then add a **Shopify Access Token** credential. Select it on the trigger, **Create Staged Upload** and **Attach Video to Product**. If your app is new, also add the `write_files` scope.\n3. Open **Workflow Config** and set `shop_subdomain` (the part before `.myshopify.com`), `shopify_api_version` (a supported Admin API version, default `2026-07`), `drive_folder_id` and `slack_channel`.\n4. Add OpenAI (or swap in any chat model), Google Drive and Slack credentials.\n5. Create a test product with an image, check the run, then activate.\n\n### Customize\n- Edit the prompt in **Write Motion Prompt** to change style or tone.\n- Change the poll interval in **Wait 30s**.\n- Each image clip costs one Sisif clip; duration and resolution are fixed by Sisif for photo clips."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4ac6c8fc-c8e5-492b-85cd-e391995ad2ff",
      "name": "Note: Generate and Poll",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -180,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### Sisif render loop\nThe photo URL is sent as `image` with the motion `prompt`. Sisif fixes duration and resolution for photo clips. The loop checks `/api/videos/{id}/status/` every 30 s, exits on `READY`, `ERROR` or `REFUNDED`, and gives up after 40 checks (about 20 minutes)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ce86c5d6-e4e8-4fa5-b053-b89b52b73e32",
      "name": "Note: Attach or Fallback",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1100,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 2600,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### Deliver the video to Shopify\nShopify does not accept an external video URL. The MP4 is downloaded and measured, `stagedUploadsCreate` (resource `VIDEO`, method `POST`) returns an upload target, and **Upload to Staged Target** posts a multipart form with Shopify's parameters in their original order and the file last. Up to 12 parameters are supported; unused slots are sent as `x-ignore-*` fields, which Google Cloud Storage ignores. `productUpdate` then adds the video to the product using the returned `resourceUrl`, and Shopify processes it for a few minutes. If any step fails, the MP4 goes to Google Drive and Slack gets the link."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
